  "id": "Compound::DB00393 - Gene::782",
  "verbalization": "Nimodipine is implicated in the regulation of high voltage-gated calcium channel activity through its interaction with Cacna1f and Cacna1s, which are subunits of the calcium channel complex. The evidence suggests that Nimodipine binds to these calcium channel subunits, thereby modulating their activity. This binding is linked to the participation of these subunits in the high voltage-gated calcium channel process, which is ultimately associated with Cacnb1. The integration of these pathways highlights a potential mechanism by which Nimodipine influences calcium channel function, potentially affecting cellular processes involving calcium signaling. The observed scores support a direct relationship between Nimodipine and Cacnb1, emphasizing the role of calcium channel subunits in mediating the drug's effects.",
